-- title:
--   Involutivity of Fr₂ and a generator of mathcal O_{2,n}
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a commutative domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is assumed to be a discrete valuation ring, together with an irreducible element $\pi$, such that $\mathcal O$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {π})`), the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and $(r)=(\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$. Let $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ (`Onr`) be a commutative domain of characteristic zero which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, and assume: $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$; that ideal is maximal; every $x\in\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies $p(x)\equiv 0 \pmod{\pi}$ for some monic $p\in\mathcal O[X]$; every monic $p\in\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}[X]$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$; and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$. Let $n\in\mathbb N$, write $\mathcal O_2$ for the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ on which $\mathrm{Fr}\circ\mathrm{Fr}$ agrees with the identity (the equalizer of these two $\mathcal O$-algebra maps), and let $\mathcal O_{2,n}$ be the quotient of $\mathcal O_2$ by the ideal generated by $\pi^{\,n+1}$. Let $\mathrm{Fr}_2$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of $\mathcal O_{2,n}$ such that for all $y,y'\in\mathcal O_2$ with $y'=\mathrm{Fr}(y)$ in $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ one has $\mathrm{Fr}_2(\bar y)=\bar{y'}$. The conclusion is twofold: $\mathrm{Fr}_2(\mathrm{Fr}_2(z))=z$ for every $z\in\mathcal O_{2,n}$; and there exists $\alpha\in\mathcal O_{2,n}$ such that $\mathrm{Fr}_2(\alpha)-\alpha$ is a unit, $\mathcal O[\alpha]=\mathcal O_{2,n}$ (the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by $\alpha$ is everything), and $\alpha^{2}=s\alpha+t$ for some $s,t\in\mathcal O$.
--
--   This is the axiomatised form of the statement that the $\mathrm{Fr}^2$-fixed subring of $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is the unramified quadratic extension of $\mathcal O$, generated modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ by a Teichmüller-type element $\alpha$ satisfying a monic quadratic equation over $\mathcal O$ and moved by the residual Frobenius into a unit difference, with $\mathrm{Fr}_2$ acting as the nontrivial involution of that extension. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development to analyse $\mathcal O$-algebra endomorphisms of the level-$n$ quotients and to descend quotient maps along the fibres.
